@model string

@* Every block this plugin asks an operator to paste into a root shell renders through here, so they
   all get the same copy button and the same wrapping.

   A bare <pre>, the way core's own command blocks are written (UpdatePointOfSale, SetupLightningNode).
   Deliberately NOT <pre><code>, and deliberately no background utility:

     - BTCPay already styles pre itself - `pre { color: var(--btcpay-pre-text) }` and
       `pre, pre code { background: var(--btcpay-pre-bg) }` - which is white on near-black in BOTH
       themes. Adding bg-tile here only recolours the pre, leaving the inner code dark on top of it.
     - `pre:not(.text-wrap) code { padding: var(--btcpay-space-m) !important }` puts 16px of padding
       on an *inline* <code>. Vertical padding does not grow an inline box's line height, so once the
       content wraps, every line paints its own dark rectangle overlapping the lines above and below:
       the text is still there and still copyable, but struck through in black.
     - .text-wrap is not the escape hatch it looks like - it is `white-space: normal !important`,
       which would collapse a multi-line script onto one line.

   Hence pre-wrap inline, and overflow-wrap so the one long $BTCPAY_BASE_DIRECTORY path wraps instead
   of forcing a horizontal scrollbar. Neither affects what the copy button puts on the clipboard. *@
<div class="d-flex justify-content-end mb-2">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-secondary only-for-js clipboard-button"
            data-clipboard="@Model"
            data-clipboard-confirm="@StringLocalizer["Copied"]">
        <vc:icon symbol="actions-copy"/>
        <span class="ms-1">Copy</span>
    </button>
</div>
<pre class="p-3 mb-0" style="white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">@Model</pre>
